 {
  "id": "wa_mount_adams_pinnacle_glacier_headwall",
  "name": "Pinnacle Glacier Headwall",
  "discipline": "mountaineering",
  "grade": "Mod. Snow",
  "verdict": "SUMMIT_ONLY",
  "state": "wa",
  "peak": {
   "id": "wa_mount_adams",
   "name": "Mount Adams",
   "lat": 46.202494,
   "lng": -121.490746,
   "elevation_ft": 12276,
   "region": "Washington",
   "path": "usa.washington.wa_sw_tacoma.wa_southwest_cascades.wa_mount_adams"
  },
  "text": {
   "approach": "A free wilderness permit is self-issued at the trailhead. From the Riley Camp Trailhead, hike the Riley Camp Trail, staying off the Riley Cut-Off at the first junction, until it meets the Pacific Crest Trail. Turn south on the Pacific Crest Trail for a few minutes to Riley Creek and follow the creek up through boulders to the moraines at the foot of the Pinnacle Glacier. The headwall route begins at the base of the glacier.",
   "approach_logistics": "{\"trailhead\":\"Riley Camp Trailhead\",\"trailheadDirection\":\"From Trout Lake, drive Mt. Adams Road north about 1.3 miles, then turn left onto Forest Road 23 (Buck Creek Road) and follow it about 17.5 miles to the trailhead, which is easy to miss between mileposts 38 and 37.\"}",
   "road": null,
   "overview": "At the base the line may be obvious or not; several variations exist, so pick one. No cracks are on the route. The angle is mild at first and steep near the top. Rock bands seem stable, so objective danger looks modest. The route ends on the Pinnacle summit, an easy stroll from the main summit. Descend along the West Ridge; some parts are exposed though easy.",
   "description": null,
   "descent": null
  },
