  "text": {
   "approach": "From the Buck Creek/Trinity Trailhead, hike roughly 6 miles through old burn/fireweed forest on the Buck Creek Trail, ford Buck Creek, then climb Mount Cleator's east ridge through logged forest. Contour left around 5,500 ft onto a boot path through an 'alder tunnel,' then traverse slippery heather and blueberry slopes to the base of twin gendarmes marking the start of the ridge. Gain the crest via a loose gully (easy to mid-5th class) right of the gendarmes.",
   "approach_logistics": null,
   "road": "{\"name\":\"Chiwawa River Road (Forest Road 6200)\",\"status\":\"Closed beyond Atkinson Flat Campground since May 20, 2026 for storm damage, under Forest Service order 06-17-07-2026-11 (through December 31, 2027). The Little Giant Fire closure (order 06-17-07-2026-40), in effect September 3 through October 31, 2026 unless lifted sooner, also closes FR 6200 and the Buck Creek Trail. Verify current status with the Wenatchee River Ranger District before approaching via Trinity/Buck Creek Trailhead.\",\"driveNote\":\"From Leavenworth: US-2 west 15 mi to Coles Corner, right on WA-207 north 4.4 mi, then Chiwaw",
